{\b Locked Hypotheses}\par
H1: Recognition positively affects student trust.\par
H2: Stackability positively affects student trust.\par
H3: Industry endorsement positively affects student trust.\par
H4: Student trust positively affects perceived value.\par
H5: Recognition positively affects perceived value.\par
H6: Stackability positively affects perceived value.\par
H7: Industry endorsement positively affects perceived value.\par
H8: Student trust mediates the effect of recognition on perceived value.\par
H9: Student trust mediates the effect of stackability on perceived value.\par
H10: Student trust mediates the effect of industry endorsement on perceived value.\par
\par
{\b Locked Method}\par
- Thailand-focused\par
- student-only respondents\par
- quantitative survey experiment\par
- randomized `2 x 2 x 2` vignette design\par
- perceived value as primary outcome\par
- enrollment intention as exploratory only\par
